ettling the guests. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death—cloaked in grave habiliments and drenched in blood—enters the ballroom, paralyzing the guests with terror; when Prince Prospero confronts the intruder with a dagger, the figure calmly moves through all seven rooms, and upon being chased into the black chamber, the prince collapses dead upon contact, revealing the figure to be an empty shell, as the plague claims every reveller and the clock ceases to tick.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"Prospero\"\n    42→      ],\n    43→      \"role\": null,\n    44→      \"appearance\": null,\n    45→      \"personality\": null,\n    46→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    47→      \"descriptions\": [\n    48→        {\n    49→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a noble figure who retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to escape a deadly plague, maintaining elaborate festivities to distract from the outside horror. He exhibits boldness and aggression when confronting a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death, ultimately dying upon contact with the intruder in the black chamber.\",\n    50→          \"source_position\": 11148,\n    51→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    52→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    53→        }\n    54→      ],\n    55→      \"relationships\": {},\n    56→      \"evidence\": [\n    57→        {\n    58→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero retreats with courtiers to escape the plague\",\n    59→          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers into his sealed, abbey-like castle, where he provides endless entertainment and indulgence to ignore the outside horror.\",\n    60→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n    61→   